{"sections":{"main":{"type":"main-page","disabled":true,"settings":{"subheading":"","show_title":true,"heading_font_size":"heading-medium","show_content":true,"text_font_size":"body-small","align_text":"text-left","width":"wrapper","color_scheme":"","padding_top":50,"padding_bottom":50,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"section_hero_B4PN3y":{"type":"section-hero","blocks":{"heading_QN3FgR":{"type":"heading","settings":{"title":"Warranty Claims","heading_font_size":"heading-x-large","heading_tag":"automatic","padding_bottom":8}},"text_Ypajjg":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>As an authorized retailer, Ski Pro assists our customers with manufacturer warranty claims to ensure your gear performs as intended.<\/p>","text_font_size":"body-large","padding_bottom":8}}},"block_order":["heading_QN3FgR","text_Ypajjg"],"disabled":true,"name":"Image banner","settings":{"image_1":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/DSC04634.jpg","link":"","width":"wrapper--full","height":"screen-height-one-third","flex_align_desktop":"align--bottom-left-desktop","content_width":50,"mobile_height":"image-height--mobile","flex_align_mobile":"align--middle-center-mobile","color_scheme":"scheme-2","show_text_background":false,"overlay_type":"opacity","padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":0,"show_placeholder":true}},"section_rich_text_DH9xyh":{"type":"section-rich-text","blocks":{"subheading_DeVUrB":{"type":"subheading","settings":{"subheading":"Getting Ready","padding_bottom":16}},"heading_kx4hiQ":{"type":"heading","settings":{"title":"Preparing Your Warranty","heading_font_size":"heading-large","padding_bottom":16,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"text_rbkGi8":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>The information provided on this page is to help you as the customer gather all of the correct information that will be needed in order to submit a warranty claim through Ski Pro. <\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","padding_bottom":16}}},"block_order":["subheading_DeVUrB","heading_kx4hiQ","text_rbkGi8"],"name":"Rich text","settings":{"align_text":"text-left","width":"wrapper","color_scheme":"","overlay_type":"disabled","padding_top":100,"padding_bottom":50}},"section_divider_YKBrXc":{"type":"section-divider","name":"Divider","settings":{"show_line":true,"width":"wrapper--full-padded","color_scheme":"","padding_top":50,"padding_bottom":50}},"section_rich_text_8YPcCU":{"type":"section-rich-text","blocks":{"heading_WdUWG8":{"type":"heading","settings":{"title":"Required Information","heading_font_size":"heading-small","padding_bottom":16,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"text_e4CMxB":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>The following list are items and information that you must have in order to submit a warranty claim. Without this information, your claim could be subject to rejection. <\/p><ul><li>Proof of Purchase<\/li><li>Product Serial Number<\/li><li>Brand, Model, Year of product<\/li><li>Images of the damage, the product as a whole, and the tags if applicable<\/li><li>Contact Info: Name, Email, Phone<\/li><li>Shipping Address<\/li><\/ul>","text_font_size":"body-medium","padding_bottom":16}}},"block_order":["heading_WdUWG8","text_e4CMxB"],"name":"Rich text","settings":{"align_text":"text-left","width":"wrapper","color_scheme":"","overlay_type":"disabled","padding_top":30,"padding_bottom":0}},"section_divider_iUTeFV":{"type":"section-divider","name":"Divider","settings":{"show_line":true,"width":"wrapper--full-padded","color_scheme":"","padding_top":50,"padding_bottom":50}},"section_rich_text_BgL3wr":{"type":"section-rich-text","blocks":{"heading_69JGRB":{"type":"heading","settings":{"title":"Proof of Purchase","heading_font_size":"heading-x-small","padding_bottom":16,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"text_j6aYKt":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>If you purchased in-store, we will need an image of your original receipt from your purchase. The receipt must include the location from which the product was purchased, the date, and total amount spent<\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","padding_bottom":16}},"heading_ThaQKz":{"type":"heading","settings":{"title":"Serial Number","heading_font_size":"heading-x-small","padding_bottom":16,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"text_UTt9yw":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>Every product will have a serial number available on the gear. Clothing may not and you may input the model number for the item if a serial number is not available. <\/p><p>For most skis and snowboards, you can usually fund the serial number engraved into the sidewall of the gear or sometimes printed on the top sheet in the middle of the ski.<\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","padding_bottom":16}},"subheading_bXtA8B":{"type":"subheading","disabled":true,"settings":{"subheading":"What's Typically Covered?","padding_bottom":16}},"subheading_MYhYXM":{"type":"subheading","disabled":true,"settings":{"subheading":"What's Not covered.","padding_bottom":16}},"text_ACNq3m":{"type":"text","disabled":true,"settings":{"text":"<p>Manufacturers <strong>will not cover<\/strong> damage due to negligence or impact related issues, including but not limited to the following. <\/p><p><\/p><ul><li>Damages due to any impact caused by sharp items, torsion, compression, a fall, an abnormal impact or other actions that cannot be under the manufacturers reasonable control.<\/li><li>Any damage to snowboard binding highbacks, including damage caused while loading ski lifts.<\/li><li>Impact damage showing scrapes, gouges, cracked or bent edges.<\/li><li>Damage caused by the contact of other objects or repetitive use on park features.<\/li><li>Damage due to transportation storage, or rust.<\/li><li>Cosmetic issues including topsheet chipping or peeling along edges due to contact with other riders. <\/li><li>Boot damage from resting a board on top while riding the lifts.<\/li><li>Ripped, torn, cut or abraded fabric.<\/li><\/ul>","text_font_size":"body-medium","padding_bottom":16}}},"block_order":["heading_69JGRB","text_j6aYKt","heading_ThaQKz","text_UTt9yw","subheading_bXtA8B","subheading_MYhYXM","text_ACNq3m"],"name":"Rich text","settings":{"align_text":"text-left","width":"wrapper","color_scheme":"","overlay_type":"disabled","padding_top":30,"padding_bottom":0}},"section_columns_xHxPbb":{"type":"section-columns","blocks":{"image_Y9PrzW":{"type":"image","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Artboard_1_71c62e9a-f174-487f-8130-eaac22829ad2.png","image_width":100,"image_shape":"normal","title":"","heading_font_size":"heading-mini","text":"<p>Base separation<\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","button_text":"","button_url":"","button_type":"btn--primary","button_size":"btn--small","button_style":"btn--solid","show_arrow":false,"image_aspect_ratio":1,"mobile_image_aspect_ratio":1,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"image_BLtpf6":{"type":"image","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Artboard_2_65b3d438-9e11-4b28-9b35-9ae18a2f63bd.png","image_width":100,"image_shape":"normal","title":"","heading_font_size":"heading-small","text":"<p>Top sheet separation<\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","button_text":"","button_url":"","button_type":"btn--primary","button_size":"","button_style":"btn--solid","show_arrow":false,"image_aspect_ratio":1,"mobile_image_aspect_ratio":1,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"image_WTrLAy":{"type":"image","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Artboard_4_3279eb5a-67d3-484e-ae5b-60830fc66fc2.png","image_width":100,"image_shape":"normal","title":"","heading_font_size":"heading-small","text":"<p>Top sheet delamination<\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","button_text":"","button_url":"","button_type":"btn--primary","button_size":"","button_style":"btn--solid","show_arrow":false,"image_aspect_ratio":1,"mobile_image_aspect_ratio":1,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"image_jVkLbi":{"type":"image","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Artboard_3_adb06c31-cbce-4030-8f7b-7b55631e57c9.png","image_width":100,"image_shape":"normal","title":"","heading_font_size":"heading-small","text":"<p>Blown out seams<\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","button_text":"","button_url":"","button_type":"btn--primary","button_size":"","button_style":"btn--solid","show_arrow":false,"image_aspect_ratio":1,"mobile_image_aspect_ratio":1,"heading_tag":"automatic"}}},"block_order":["image_Y9PrzW","image_BLtpf6","image_WTrLAy","image_jVkLbi"],"name":"Text columns with images","settings":{"title":"","heading_font_size":"heading-medium","align_heading":"text-left","align_text":"text-left","width":"wrapper","align_columns":"flex-align-center","layout":"grid","grid":3,"layout_mobile":"2","color_scheme":"","padding_top":50,"padding_bottom":50,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"section_rich_text_E3FznB":{"type":"section-rich-text","blocks":{"heading_pEm6aM":{"type":"heading","settings":{"title":"What's Not covered","heading_font_size":"heading-small","padding_bottom":16,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"subheading_bB8RnV":{"type":"subheading","disabled":true,"settings":{"subheading":"Warranty Details","padding_bottom":16}},"text_TNPhQr":{"type":"text","disabled":true,"settings":{"text":"<p>At Ski Pro, we act as your advocate by facilitating warranty claims between you and the manufacturer. Please note that <strong>shipping costs to send the product to Ski Pro or the manufacturer for  inspection are the customer's responsibility.<\/strong> If the manufacturer approves your claim, we will cover the return shipping for your repaired or replaced item (within the U.S.). For approved claims that can be fixed with parts, we will provide those directly or request them from the brand. Please be aware that external costs—such as lift tickets, rentals, or mounting fees—are not covered by Ski Pro or the manufacturer.<\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","padding_bottom":16}},"subheading_wdCAF8":{"type":"subheading","disabled":true,"settings":{"subheading":"What's Typically Covered?","padding_bottom":16}},"text_N8Ccnz":{"type":"text","disabled":true,"settings":{"text":"<p>A manufacturers warranty typically covers defects due to the manufacturing process and can include the following.<\/p><p><\/p><ul><li>Top sheet, base or sidewall delamination due to manufacturing defect.<\/li><li>Manufacturing defect resulting in cracking on the top sheet, base, sidewall or edge.<\/li><li>Misaligned, spinning inserts. Please be aware that stripped inserts or damage to the insert or base due to improper mounting is not considered a material flaw and is not repairable.<\/li><li>Seam seperation, zipper malfunctions, button and clasp issues on clothing articles.<\/li><\/ul>","text_font_size":"body-medium","padding_bottom":16}},"subheading_aBFqrU":{"type":"subheading","disabled":true,"settings":{"subheading":"What's Not covered.","padding_bottom":16}},"text_MXX3YC":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>Manufacturers <strong>will not cover<\/strong> damage due to negligence or impact related issues, including but not limited to the following. <\/p><p><\/p><ul><li>Damages due to any impact caused by sharp items, torsion, compression, a fall, an abnormal impact or other actions that cannot be under the manufacturers reasonable control.<\/li><li>Any damage to snowboard binding highbacks, including damage caused while loading ski lifts.<\/li><li>Impact damage showing scrapes, gouges, cracked or bent edges.<\/li><li>Damage caused by the contact of other objects or repetitive use on park features.<\/li><li>Damage due to transportation storage, or rust.<\/li><li>Cosmetic issues including topsheet chipping or peeling along edges due to contact with other riders. <\/li><li>Boot damage from resting a board on top while riding the lifts.<\/li><li>Ripped, torn, cut or abraded fabric.<\/li><\/ul>","text_font_size":"body-medium","padding_bottom":16}}},"block_order":["heading_pEm6aM","subheading_bB8RnV","text_TNPhQr","subheading_wdCAF8","text_N8Ccnz","subheading_aBFqrU","text_MXX3YC"],"disabled":true,"name":"Rich text","settings":{"align_text":"text-left","width":"wrapper","color_scheme":"","overlay_type":"disabled","padding_top":30,"padding_bottom":0}},"section_rich_text_columns_a3BE8n":{"type":"section-rich-text-columns","blocks":{"heading_jHqQQA":{"type":"heading","settings":{"title":"In Store Support","heading_font_size":"heading-large","position":"left","padding_bottom":16,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"text_yCxWwJ":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>Connect with our stores for expert gear recommendations, Inventory availability, fitting and sizing, and help with rentals or service. <\/p><p><em>Please note: in-store teams aren’t able to look up or change online orders.<\/em><\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","position":"left","padding_bottom":16}},"buttons_W6gGaW":{"type":"buttons","settings":{"position":"left","button_text":"Store Details","button_url":"shopify:\/\/pages\/locations","button_type":"btn--primary","button_size":"","button_style":"btn--solid","show_arrow":false,"button_secondary_text":"","button_secondary_url":"","button_secondary_type":"btn--primary","button_secondary_size":"","button_secondary_style":"btn--outline","show_secondary_arrow":false,"padding_bottom":16}},"heading_4JTP7f":{"type":"heading","settings":{"title":"Phoenix Metro Area","heading_font_size":"heading-large","position":"right","padding_bottom":16,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"text_EWzagD":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"{{ metaobjects.location.mesa.hours | metafield_tag }}<p><em>Hours of <\/em>operations <em>are subject to change<\/em><\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","position":"right","padding_bottom":16}},"heading_eLneQC":{"type":"heading","settings":{"title":"Phoenix & Avalanche Outlet","heading_font_size":"heading-small","position":"right","padding_bottom":16,"heading_tag":"automatic"}},"text_B9mCkX":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p><strong>Address:<\/strong> 2110 East Camelback Road, Phoenix, Arizona 85016<\/p><p><strong>Direct Phone:<\/strong> <a href=\"tel:6029553939\" title=\"tel:6029553939\">602-955-3939<\/a><\/p>","text_font_size":"body-medium","position":"right","padding_